From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LuneOS / webOS Ports <team@webos-ports.org>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] CMakeLists: pass library dirs, not library names, to
 link_directories

link_directories() takes directories, but it was being given
GSTREAMER_LIBRARIES - the pkg-config library *names* (gstreamer-1.0,
gstplayer-1.0, glib-2.0, gobject-2.0, gstvideo-1.0, gstbase-1.0). CMake treats
those as relative paths and resolves them against the source directory, so the
build ends up with link paths inside the source tree, which then land in the
binary's RPATH:

  QA Issue: g-media-pipeline-clang: /usr/lib/cbe/libgmp-player-client.so.1.0
  contains bad RPATH .../sources/g-media-pipeline-clang-1.0.0-gav.59/gstplayer-1.0:...
  QA Issue: File /usr/lib/cbe/libgmp-player-client.so.1.0 ... contains
  reference to TMPDIR [buildpaths]

pkg_check_modules() already exports GSTPLAYER_LIBRARY_DIRS and
GSTREAMER_LIBRARY_DIRS for exactly this; the per-target CMakeLists under src/
already use the _LIBRARY_DIRS form. This makes the top level consistent and
removes both QA issues at their source rather than scrubbing the RPATH
afterwards.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -46,7 +46,7 @@
 set(GSTREAMER_LIBRARIES ${GSTPLAYER_LIBRARIES} ${GSTREAMER_LIBRARIES})
 
 include_directories(${GSTREAMER_INCLUDE_DIRS})
-link_directories(${GSTREAMER_LIBRARIES})
+link_directories(${GSTPLAYER_LIBRARY_DIRS} ${GSTREAMER_LIBRARY_DIRS})
 
 if(${WEBOS_TARGET_MACHINE} STREQUAL "qemux86" OR ${WEBOS_TARGET_MACHINE} STREQUAL "qemux86-64")
     add_definitions(-DPLATFORM_QEMUX86)
